Resource    taf/rfrl/procedures/resources/robot/RfScan.robot

*** Keywords ***
General_SiSo_Auto_TEST_RF_Sniffing_RF_Scanning
    [Documentation]
    ...     The purpose of the test is to check if the RF Scan procedure is working properly.
    ...     The procedure can be found via WEBEM: Diagnostic -> RF Monitoring -> RF Scan.
    ...     The feature is activated if parameter actRfiTesting value is True.
    ...     Main steps of the test case look like:
    ...       1) setting actRfiTesting to False
    ...       2) checking unavailability of start RF Scan (should not be available)
    ...       3) setting actRfiTesting to True
    ...       4) starting RF Scan test
    ...       5) verifying RF Scan result file (name + file size)
    ...     Step 4 and 5 is repeated for every configuration.
    ...
    ...     ARGS:
    ...     :param dict radio_supported_capture_types: (Mandatory) :
    ...            Should be set to None when rf_scan_custom_parameters is used. Key is the name of radio and
    ...            value is a list of supported capture types for this radio. A dictionary should contains every radio
    ...            included in used configuration.
    ...            The capture types for radio can be found in BPF Tool (property names: 'Support.RfScanning.(...)').
    ...            Example:
    ...            {'AEHC': ['Carrier Rx (FIR9)', 'Raw Composite Rx (RxADC)'],
    ...             'AHPE': ['Carrier Rx (FIR9)', 'Composite Rx (HBF0)']}
    ...            Allowed capture types: 'Carrier Rx (FIR9)', 'Raw Composite Rx (RxADC)', 'Composite Rx (HBF0)',
    ...                                   'Feedback Tx (PDRx)'(only in R&D mode not supported by the test).
    ...     :param list of dicts rf_scan_custom_parameters: (Optional) :
    ...            Need to be set if the test should not use generated list of dictionary for input data on the basis
    ...            of radio_supported_capture_types. Only specific input data from rf_scan_custom_parameters will be
    ...            used during the test.
    ...            Example:
    ...            [{'radio': 'RMOD-2 (AHPE)', 'capture_type': 'Carrier Rx (FIR9)', 'technology': 'LTE FDD',
    ...             'local_cell': 'LNCEL-2', 'antenna_panel': None, 'antenna': 'ANT 2'},
    ...             {'radio': 'RMOD-2 (AHPE)', 'capture_type': 'Composite Rx (HBF0)', 'technology': 'LTE FDD',
    ...             'local_cell': None, 'antenna_panel': None, 'antenna': 'ANT 2'},
    ...             {'radio': 'RMOD-1 (AEHC)', 'capture_type': 'Carrier Rx (FIR9)', 'technology': 'NR TDD',
    ...             'local_cell': 'NRCELL-1', 'antenna_panel': 'PHYANT-1 Full Array', 'antenna': 'PHYANT 1'},
    ...             {'radio': 'RMOD-1 (AEHC)', 'capture_type': 'Composite Rx (HBF0)', 'technology': 'NR TDD',
    ...             'local_cell': None, 'antenna_panel': 'PHYANT-1 Full Array', 'antenna': 'PHYANT 1'}]

    [Arguments]                                         ${radio_supported_capture_types}
    ...                                                 ${rf_scan_custom_parameters}=${None}
    [Timeout]                                           24 hours

    ${RF_Scan_path}                                     Set variable    ${logs_path}/RF_Scan_Files
    ${RF_Scan_path_download}                            Set variable    ${RF_Scan_path}/RF_Scan_Download
    Create RF Scan Files Directory                      RF_Scan_path=${RF_Scan_path}
    ...                                                 RF_Scan_path_download=${RF_Scan_path_download}

    ${bts_type}=                                        hwpta_testline.get_type_of_setup
    Create admin session with default alias             bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${connection}=                                      connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias
    ...                                                 bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${webui_obj}                                        Create Selenium Session
    ...                                                 admin_connection=${connection}
    ...                                                 download_dir=${RF_Scan_path_download}
    config_operations.connect                           alias=${connection}

    ${rf_scan_input_data}=                              Run keyword if      ${rf_scan_custom_parameters}
    ...                                                 Set variable
    ...                                                 ${rf_scan_custom_parameters}
    ...                                                 ELSE
    ...                                                 Create Input Data For RF Scan
    ...                                                 connection=${connection}
    ...                                                 radio_supported_capture_types=${radio_supported_capture_types}

    ${rf_scan_feature_param}=                           Get RF Scan Feature Parameter
    Run Keyword If                                      '${rf_scan_feature_param}'=='true'
    ...                                                 Set RF Scan Feature Parameter To True/False
    ...                                                 param_value=false

    ${first_entry_data}=	                            Get From List	${rf_scan_input_data}   0
    Check If RF Scanning Is Not Available               rf_scan_parameters_dict=${first_entry_data}
    ...                                                 webui_obj=${webui_obj}

    Set RF Scan Feature Parameter To True/False         param_value=true

    FOR  ${rf_scan_input_entry}  IN  @{rf_scan_input_data}
        Start RF Scanning And Validate Result File
        ...                                                 rf_scan_parameters_dict=${rf_scan_input_entry}
        ...                                                 RF_Scan_path=${RF_Scan_path}
        ...                                                 RF_Scan_path_download=${RF_Scan_path_download}
        Sleep   1m 5s
    END

    Run keyword and ignore error                        Connections.Close Selenium Session
